# Root crontab of the multi-product-bot VM - the LIVE text, as `sudo crontab -l`
# printed it on 2026-10-27 at about 19:00 UTC in Oracle Cloud Shell
# (transcribed from the screen). Everything below this header is that text,
# line for line. It is the record of what runs: refresh it after any change on
# the VM, and dump the live one again before any edit or rebuild. From Cloud
# Shell, where the key ~/mp_vm_key lives:
#     ssh -i ~/mp_vm_key opc@<vm-ip> 'sudo crontab -l'
#
# How to read it. Each CRON_TZ line sets the clock for the lines below it.
#   * */15 ensure_gateway.sh comes before any CRON_TZ (the VM's own clock). It
#     and the weekly_reauth / reauth_check lines are from the IB Gateway era
#     (WIKI.md "Leftovers from the IB Gateway era"); the bot trades over the
#     Web API (IB_BACKEND=web).
#   * The trading run alone is pinned to UTC (since 2026-09-25): 35 23 = 23:35
#     UTC all year. It pulls code itself first (git fetch, git reset --hard
#     origin/main), runs with HK_ENABLED=1, and on success touches
#     /root/ran_<UTC date> - the date taken when the run ENDS, so a run that
#     ends after midnight UTC marks the next day.
#   * That marker carries the UTC date of the evening, so the next morning's
#     10:00 London catch-up (/root/monday_catchup.sh: 09:00 UTC in summer,
#     10:00 UTC in winter) finds none for its own date and runs EVERY day, as
#     a second trading run; on success it touches the marker itself, and the
#     12:00 London line - its retry - then exits at once.
#   * The catch-up does NOT git pull: it runs the checkout the :25 publish line
#     last reset to origin/main (see monday_catchup.sh beside this file, which
#     also has no HK_ENABLED=1 in the 2026-10-27 reading).
#   * Europe/London lines move an hour in UTC with the UK clocks: the digest
#     40 23 is 22:40 UTC in summer (before the 23:35 run) and 23:40 UTC in
#     winter (five minutes after it); :25 and the every-N-minutes lines are
#     the same either way.
# A reference copy, not an install file.
*/15 * * * * /root/ensure_gateway.sh
CRON_TZ=Europe/London
0 10 * * * /root/monday_catchup.sh
0 12 * * * /root/monday_catchup.sh
25 8 * * 1 /root/weekly_reauth.sh
30 8 * * * /root/reauth_check.sh
30 9 * * * /root/reauth_check.sh
0 11 * * 1 /root/reauth_check.sh
CRON_TZ=UTC
35 23 * * * cd /root/multi-product-signals && git fetch origin main -q && git reset --hard origin/main -q; cd /root/multi-product-signals/execution && IB_BACKEND=web IB_PORT=4001 CONFIRM_FIRST=0 HK_ENABLED=1 python3.11 ib_bot.py >> /root/bot.log 2>&1 && touch /root/ran_$(date -u +\%F)
CRON_TZ=Europe/London
25 * * * * cd /root/multi-product-signals && git fetch origin main -q && git reset --hard origin/main -q; cd execution && /usr/bin/python3 publish_web.py >> /root/publish.log 2>&1
*/10 * * * * cd /root/multi-product-signals/execution && IB_BACKEND=web IB_PORT=4001 python3.11 ib_commands.py >> /root/commands.log 2>&1
40 23 * * * cd /root/multi-product-signals/execution && HK_ENABLED=1 /usr/bin/python3 daily_signal.py >> /root/daily_signal.log 2>&1
*/2 * * * * cd /root/multi-product-signals/execution && /usr/bin/python3 telegram_poll.py >> /root/tg.log 2>&1
